; Ported from dot_config/private_pet/snippet.nu.toml.
;
; Nushell-only: these are nu pipelines, not POSIX shell, so they are kept out
; of ../cheats (which zsh reads) the same way pet kept them out of
; snippet.toml. The nushell `navi` wrapper in dot_config/nushell/function.nu
; passes `--path` for this directory; zsh never sees these cheats.
;
; The `$ var:` suggestion lines below run under `shell.command` from
; config.yaml, which is left at navi's default of bash - that key has no CLI or
; environment override. Plain `echo` is portable, so it does not matter here; a
; nu-native suggestion (`ls *.csv | get name`) would need its own config file
; with `shell: {command: nu}`, selected via NAVI_CONFIG.

% nu, csv, yaml, filter

# filter CSV rows and write them out as YAML
```nu
open <file>
| where status == "<status>"
| where score >= <min_score>
| select name email score
| sort-by score --reverse
| to yaml
```

$ file: echo 'data.csv'
$ status: echo 'active'
$ min_score: echo '80'

% nu, sqlite, vipe, atuin, query

# run SQL query against atuin DB.
```nu
let sql = (vipe --suffix sql)
open <db> | query db $sql
```

$ db: echo '~/.local/share/atuin/history.db'
